    "description": "Dames Point Jacksonville LLC is the local operating and concession entity associated with JAXPORT's 158-acre Dames Point container terminal and adjacent intermodal container transfer facility in Jacksonville, Florida. The business handles container, stevedoring, crane, yard and rail-transfer activity for ocean carriers, cargo owners and military users under long-term port rights. Ceres acquired the former TraPac Jacksonville entity in 2022; Macquarie retained the renamed local SPV when the broader Ceres platform was sold to Carrix, then sold the Jacksonville business and assets separately to JAXPORT in November 2023. JAXPORT is the current owner and SSA is the contract operator, not an equity owner.",
